<title>TURKEY: Ege Biracilik 9-mth profits up slightly.</title>
<headline>Ege Biracilik 9-mth profits up slightly.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  938.53  vs     924.78</p>
<p>    Net profit			 1,479.60  vs   1,457.93</p>
<p>    Net sales			  8,358.27  vs   3,710.25</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 2,008.33  vs   1,481.21</p>
<p>    Exceptional income		 811.03  vs     372.18</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    1,048.30  vs	12.88</p>
<p>    Total debts			5,101.66  vs   2,044.14</p>
<p>    Equity			     7,064.15  vs   3,924.72</p>
<p>    Capital			    1,576.51  vs   1,576.51</p>
<p>NOTE - Brewer Ege Biracilik ve Malt Sanayi A.S. is largely owned by Turkish brewery, automotive and stationery group Anadolu Endustri Holding. It produces leading beer brand Efes Pilsen with four other breweries and malt producers within the same group.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
